# The working tree is CRLF on Windows (see .prettierrc), which is fine for
# everything the toolchain reads - except a shell script the container runs.
# With CRLF the shebang ends in \r and Linux answers "sh: not found".
*.sh text eol=lf

# Save fixtures are binary. Without this git treats them as text on a CRLF
# working tree and rewrites bytes on checkout, which corrupts the fixture in a
# way that only shows up as a parse failure.
*.sav binary
